```python
score = int(input("Enter score: "))
if score >= 90:
    print("Excellent")
elif score >= 75:
    print("Good")
elif score >= 60:
    print("Average")
elif score >= 40:
    print("Needs Improvement")
else:
    print("Fail")
```
For `score = 74`: first condition false (74>=90), second false (74>=75), third true (74>=60) → prints "Average". A wrong trace (e.g., printing "Good") indicates the student incorrectly ordered the conditions (e.g., put `>=60` before `>=75`) or thinks multiple blocks can execute.

