A student wrote the following code to classify a triangle by sides (equilateral, isosceles, scalene). Identify the logical error and correct it.
```python
a = int(input("Side a: "))
b = int(input("Side b: "))
c = int(input("Side c: "))
if a == b:
    if b == c:
        print("Equilateral")
    else:
        print("Isosceles")
elif b == c:
    print("Isosceles")
elif a == c:
    print("Isosceles")
else:
    print("Scalene")
```

